@page
@model BeeMemoryBank.Web.Pages.Admin.BlindNodesModel

@section About {
    <p>
        A <strong>blind node</strong> is a machine that keeps an encrypted copy of this network and of its backups, and cannot read any of it: it never holds the key. It is an
        off-site safe for your data. If every full node were lost, the blind node still holds what a restore needs; only you can open it, with your master password.
    </p>
    <p>
        To let a friend keep a copy on their own device (the <strong>Blind copy</strong> app on a phone, a PC or a Mac), make an <strong>invitation</strong> on the Blind nodes page:
        you get one line of text and a QR code that work once, for a few minutes. Send them to your friend by a channel you trust. Their app asks to join and shows a
        short <strong>match code</strong>; you compare it with the one on this page and confirm with your master password. Until you confirm, no vault content and no usable key of your memory bank is sent to their device.
        Asking to join already sends this node their device id, public key, name, platform, version and their own backup key; the node keeps that backup key encrypted until you decide. You
        can withdraw an invitation that has not been used.
    </p>
    <p>
        The older way is the <strong>pair code</strong>, and it is the only way for a blind node on a server (Docker or a service): its own console shows the code, and you paste it on the
        Blind nodes page. This PC checks the node's key, checks that every other device already sees this PC as a superadmin and runs a current version, and then sends the
        node its first copy. A phone in &ldquo;Blind copy&rdquo; mode can still be added the older way too, with the &ldquo;Add an Android blind copy&rdquo; link on that page. On the Blind nodes page you can see each blind copy's
        status and alarms, reseed a blind node (send it a fresh copy) or disconnect it.
    </p>
    <p>
        The page also lists the <em>hubs</em> for blind copies: the full nodes a blind copy (on a PC, a Mac or a phone) is allowed to call. You set a hub up under
        <a href="/Admin/TrustedNodes">Trusted Nodes</a>, with &ldquo;Let blind copies call this node&rdquo;.
    </p>
}

<div class="card mt-md" style="max-width:640px;">
    <sl-button variant="primary" size="small" href="/BlindNodes">
        <sl-icon slot="prefix" name="shield-lock"></sl-icon> Blind nodes
    </sl-button>
</div>
